WEBVTT

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:12.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the fourteenth, September. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:14.169 --> 00:00:19.070
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, you're there. Anyone watch the football last night? Honestly, that last ten minutes.</v>

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:24.030
<v Callum Reid>Unfortunately. Ten minutes of my life I'm not getting back.</v>

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:31.000
<v Hannah Price>Oh, come on, you were probably shouting at the telly like the rest of us.</v>

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:40.469
<v Aisha Begum>Never mind that, the broken coffee machine in the canteen has properly ruined my morning. Just having a moan, not putting a job in.</v>

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.500
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That explains the atmosphere. Seven people running on residual caffeine.</v>

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:49.450
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a support group. Where did nights leave us?</v>

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:55.740
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, finished the repair on the heater box on one last night. That's done.</v>

00:00:57.219 --> 00:01:00.369
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Closed off, then, not another one for today.</v>

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:07.840
<v Callum Reid>And I already swapped the filter on the Injection Moulding Line 3 yesterday. That one's finished as well.</v>

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:14.700
<v Aisha Begum>That's the line filter you're talking about, yeah? Not the other filter we've been discussing?</v>

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.140
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, the Injection Moulding Line 3. Separate job, already done.</v>

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:26.219
<v Sarah Okafor>On the outstanding one, I'll swap the filter on the power pack on one by Wednesday. It's urgent.</v>

00:01:27.989 --> 00:01:31.840
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Okay, boss, you've got the power pack on one filter, then?</v>

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.799
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, mine. By Wednesday, and keep it marked urgent.</v>

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:43.510
<v Aisha Begum>Just on nights, I noticed the Atlas was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.629
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Settled right back, or just stopped climbing?</v>

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.459
<v Aisha Begum>Right back. Just an observation, nothing outstanding from that.</v>

00:01:52.890 --> 00:02:00.239
<v Callum Reid>Similar sort of thing, saw the pressure on the Arburg dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:02:01.209 --> 00:02:04.010
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, both observations, no new jobs off those.</v>

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:10.449
<v Hannah Price>And I tested the trucks yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished.</v>

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:14.169
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, you said yesterday? You broke up a bit.</v>

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:18.069
<v Hannah Price>Yesterday, yeah. Testing's done, all fine.</v>

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:23.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Separate from that completed testing, I'll do the pre-use checks on the counterbalances tomorrow.</v>

00:02:25.509 --> 00:02:28.659
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, boss. The counterbalances pre-use checks tomorrow, got you.</v>

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.710
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. Not reopening yesterday's testing.</v>

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:39.020
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team this morning? Low priority, that one.</v>

00:02:39.889 --> 00:02:45.490
<v Jamie Brennan>Um, sorry, I can't take the toolbox talk. I can't commit to organising it this morning.</v>

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:54.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Pricey, can you take it instead? Organise the toolbox talk for the team this morning. Still low priority.</v>

00:02:55.830 --> 00:03:01.430
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll take that off Jamie. I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team this morning.</v>

00:03:01.909 --> 00:03:06.810
<v Aisha Begum>Low priority, but still this morning, just so we're not hearing two different things?</v>

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:13.469
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. This morning is still the timing; it's not an urgent one.</v>

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:19.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, can you inspect the water booster for leaks today as well?</v>

00:03:20.219 --> 00:03:23.370
<v Hannah Price>Yep, I'll inspect the water booster for leaks today.</v>

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:29.400
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That's an inspection, yeah? We're not saying there's a repair agreed?</v>

00:03:31.159 --> 00:03:34.310
<v Hannah Price>Correct, just inspecting for leaks. No repair being added.</v>

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:42.500
<v Sarah Okafor>And Hannah Price, can you chase the purchase order for the Fire Alarm Panel first thing tomorrow?</v>

00:03:44.139 --> 00:03:49.039
<v Hannah Price>Yes, I'll chase the purchase order for the Fire Alarm Panel first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:56.550
<v Jamie Brennan>Right, that's the purchase order chase. Separate from the parts we're still stuck waiting for.</v>

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:05.740
<v Hannah Price>Yeah. I'm still waiting on parts for the long belt, nothing we can do until they arrive. That remains blocked.</v>

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:13.509
<v Jamie Brennan>Same with the MV01. Still waiting on parts for the MV01, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:04:14.669 --> 00:04:18.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Both stay blocked, then. We're not assigning any work on those today.</v>

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:29.970
<v Aisha Begum>There's also the need to grease and check the bearings on the newer turbine first thing tomorrow. Not an emergency but don't let it slip. Anyone able to take that?</v>

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:34.410
<v Callum Reid>I can't put my name against that, sorry.</v>

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:37.259
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, I can't commit to it either.</v>

00:04:39.019 --> 00:04:48.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, grease and check the bearings on the newer turbine, first thing tomorrow. Not an emergency but don't let it slip. That's still needing an owner.</v>

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.449
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, not one I can take on.</v>

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:58.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Nobody's taken it. Leave it visibly unowned, not against someone just because they've spoken.</v>

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:04.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you send the shift handover report round, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:12.589
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, that I can take. I'll send the shift handover report round if I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:05:14.879 --> 00:05:17.680
<v Callum Reid>The existing report, we're talking? Not another version?</v>

00:05:18.279 --> 00:05:21.430
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, just sending the existing one round. No rewrite.</v>

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:27.240
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll run the monthly fire alarm test by Thursday as well.</v>

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:31.470
<v Hannah Price>Thanks, Saz. Monthly fire alarm test with you, by Thursday.</v>

00:05:33.029 --> 00:05:36.879
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right. Separate from the Fire Alarm Panel purchase order chase.</v>

00:05:39.139 --> 00:05:48.240
<v Priya Raman>And I'll update the risk assessment for work on the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve at half two. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:53.040
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, that's the production hold-up. It does need doing first.</v>

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:58.120
<v Priya Raman>Understood. At half two, and that update comes first. I'm taking it.</v>

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:06.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, PR. The risk assessment for work on the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve is yours at half two, with that production priority.</v>

00:06:08.189 --> 00:06:11.689
<v Aisha Begum>And that doesn't change the urgent filter timing, does it?</v>

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:17.680
<v Sarah Okafor>No. The power pack on one filter is still urgent, by Wednesday. Neither timing's moved.</v>

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:24.480
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, someone came over you then— Teams has decided we only get one syllable each.</v>

00:06:25.569 --> 00:06:30.470
<v Jamie Brennan>I heard it. Neither timing's moved. Very economical meeting if we only get syllables.</v>

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.519
<v Hannah Price>Nothing else from me beyond what we've covered.</v>

00:06:34.949 --> 00:06:39.149
<v Callum Reid>Same here. Just glad the finished stuff isn't getting rolled over again.</v>

00:06:41.139 --> 00:06:44.990
<v Aisha Begum>And the coffee complaint remains a complaint, before anyone gets clever.</v>

00:06:47.449 --> 00:06:48.850
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Wouldn't dream of it.</v>

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's us. Cheers, everyone.</v>
